                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "its unfair on its normal difficulty, but that's the point. you're someone with little power and a lot of responsibility, who was elected to be a scapegoat. there is an easier difficulty setting too, which i appreciate. really good detective/management game, makes your choices seem really meaningful because sometimes there's no right answer, and sometimes the best course of action is to not investigate a mystery. really feels like a noir. everyone's morally gray, you don't know who to trust, and at the start of the game there is always one randomly-selected traitor that you have to unmask. the artstyle's inconsistent but it does get the point across. i recommend going to settings and clicking the help button to see the game's manual, it is really useful.\n\nas of writing this, its on sale for $5, so you should absolutely buy this at this price.",
